ORDINANCE NO. 523AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE CITY OFRECTOR, ARKANSAS, TO REGULATE THE CLEANINGOF BUILDINGS AND RESIDENCES THAT HAVE BEENDECLARED A NUISANCE BY THE CITY OF RECTORDUE TO SUBSTANTIAL FIRE DAMAGE ORDESTRUCTIONWHEREAS, it is necessary for the City of Rector, Arkansas, to monitor theappearance of all property and to prevent any property from becoming a hazard or anuisance within the citv: andNOW THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED BY THE CITY COUNCILOF THE CITY OF RECTOR. ARKANSAS. AS FOLLOWS:Section l: The City Superintendent shall notify the City Council of anystructures that have sustained substantial fire damage or destruction within the city limitsat the next subsequent Council meeting.Section 2: The City Superintendent shall notify the owner of the property bycertified mail, restricted delivery or personal service of the owner's responsibility withinthis ordinance.Section 3: The owner of the house, building and/or structure shall be given 90days, from receipt of the letter, to remove and or dispose of the same in such a manner asdeemed appropriate by the Rector Street Department and Rector City Council.Section 4: If the house, building and/structure constituting a nuisance has notbeen torn down and removed, or otherwise remedied as requested by the Rector CityCouncil, the City Council may designate the City Superintendent to tear down andremove any such house, building, and/or structure. The City of Rector may seek
-l-

